# fdfpv-metrics.service: one minute of the VM's history for the admin page
# (tracks-api/collect.js, into /var/lib/fdfpv-metrics/metrics.db), run by
# fdfpv-metrics.timer. Installed by deploy/vm/install.sh.
#
# Why a unit of its own and not the tracks server: the Server section
# wants the journal's warnings, the sizes of Postgres's and the servers'
# 0700 state directories, Caddy's certificate dates and systemctl's
# restart counts. Giving those to the tracks server would widen the
# sandbox of a process that faces the internet. This one listens on
# nothing, talks only to loopback, and writes only its own directory.
#
# What it is given beyond the tracks unit's sandbox, each for one reason:
#   - SupplementaryGroups=systemd-journal: reading the journal, which is
#     what that group is for (journalctl -p warning; lines are masked
#     before they are stored, tracks-api/metrics.js mask).
#   - CAP_DAC_READ_SEARCH, ambient, for a user with no other capability:
#     read and list past file permissions, never write, for the sizes of
#     /var/lib/pgsql, /var/lib/fdfpv-* and /var/log/journal and for
#     /var/lib/caddy's certificates. ProtectSystem=strict keeps every path
#     but its StateDirectory read only regardless.
# Group fdfpv-tracks, a 0750 directory and UMask 0027: the tracks server
# reads the store (read only, metrics.js serverReport) and nobody else
# does. ADMIN_SECRET from tracks.env asks the rooms and tracks servers for
# their last minute over loopback.
